From dd9a3b3b6b3bdab9d2a401d89d4e74ed51910414 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@buttzeppelin>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:10:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Zeppelin F-223: ZepModernM2 bone-budget split, profile clamp,
 index start repair

- every skin with a section over 75 bones is split into sub-sections that fit the vertex
  shader bone palette (constant 31 + 3 per bone); batches repeated per sub-section
- 3.3.5 files declaring more than 4 skin profiles use profile 0 (stock reads before the table)
- skins over 65535 indices with dropped level halves get their wrapped starts restored
- modern sections past 65535 are drawn instead of parked

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ByrZ7GxoHC9wfGdkRwtqCX
